          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "conclure came into Old French as conclure, a borrowing from Latin conclūdere \"to shut up, to bring to an end\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), built on claudere \"to shut\"."
